Z||000000||Mattyman||10-06-2001||01:27 PM||||I just got 2 new rear tires on my Fiero about 2 weeks ago and ever since that it seems very unstable like im riding on J-E-L-L-O.  Its kind of like those old rides at amusement parks where u have the sail to change your direction,  the car seems to be going straight while the back end twists around and the front doesnt line up with the road (hard to expalin).  Also when i hit the gas the car pulls way to the right.  My dads Astro Van seems more stable than my Fiero now(and thats real scary).  I dont know if they screwed something up or what.  Im gonna have to get it checked out.  If anyone has any idea let me know.||||reg||1
Z||000001||KissMySSFiero||10-06-2001||03:15 PM||||what kind of tires are they?  i say take the car back to where you got them put on. also what model fiero is it?   <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <BR>88FORMULA<BR>       <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>        <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DrDave||10-06-2001||03:31 PM||||The only time I experienced that was when I mixed bias tires with radial tires.   But wrong inflation can cause similar problems||||reg||1
Z||000003||tomcat06085||10-06-2001||05:24 PM||||make sure the tires aren't too big for the wheels, lug nuts are tight, no spacers added to make room for suspension....don't drive it too long like this.<P>The tire profile and tread width combo is crucial to stable handling.<P>------------------<BR>tomcat<BR>Help me go fast!||||reg||4
Z||000004||SteveJ||10-06-2001||08:11 PM||||They continue to sell those tires with only one ply in the side wall and a second under the tread. Can't see how they are safe.<P>Are they that construction?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mattyman||10-06-2001||08:40 PM||||The tires are Uniroyal Tiger Paw ASC's.  They are on my 87 coupe.  They are 195-70-R14's.  The basic size.  It seems as though the side walls arent as supportive.||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||10-06-2001||09:33 PM||||There are things is life you simply CANNOT afford to skimp on.  They are, amoung others, Tyres and brakes for your automobile.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>PS: when you got new tyres, you got a 4-wheel alignment, right? right?!  You need one if not  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
